    <item>
      <title>L298N Motor Driver</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/iot/esp/components/l298n/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/iot/esp/components/l298n/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;van-list-0&#34; class=&#34;van-img-list van-img-list-small&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;script type=&#34;module&#34;&gt;&#xA;import { renderImgYtList } from &#39;/js/img-yt-list.js&#39;;&#xA;&#xA;try {&#xA;  renderImgYtList(&#39;van-list-0&#39;, &#34;\n\n- title: L298N Motor Drive Controller Board Module Dual H Bridge DC Stepper Module\n  href: https:\/\/www.amazon.ca\/Controller-Module-Bridge-Stepper-Arduino\/dp\/B0D8G2PZBB\/ref=sr_1_3?crid=37BJ0XZPKGEDP\u0026dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.0q3Dq3VVgGpIWrot0Y7Pa1EexaxoF0-2Jxk2gG85knvSlMBbAG7nT1NXo1mGG3xoWqllSDvvPsGa0K_QWOLXdSrRfaCrLAMz7-tETDjJOr4Z-6lmY1aAHfOASs-gY-IC1qHt6-ScYAyQmOn0q8OHEWDCW4hY5-rWoHe-X0xND0E7Qt47lI1evuJfmqvnsNSZ38fK0qP4TAtWYcNI7DZniCpy-ntz3h_kTE7hlxzsTVBodVsDTyuk_JjLBu1-T3-pksGqTYZcUsvXlELriB8_Ea86z1iJiS0BTXeer9bLVGI.MHnN92jPHntJhkDLhvfR-Qirrfo4w6PiGlpe3KTOzlk\u0026dib_tag=se\u0026keywords=l298n\u0026qid=1777407138\u0026s=hi\u0026sprefix=l298n%2Ctools%2C151\u0026sr=1-3\n  img: ..\/l298n.jpg\n  text: |\n    * Use L298N as the main driving chip, so the module has such features as strong driving ability, strong anti-interference and low calorific value. And it also use large-capacity filter capacitor and diode with freewheeling protection function, thereby improve the reliability of module.\n    * No assembly required. This L298N board comes ready to go. Just wire up motors and power, this thing will work wonders.\n    * External size 43*43*27mm \/ 1.69*1.69*1.06 inch. Drive voltage 5V-35V, high working power to 46V. Large current can reach 3A MAX and continue current is 2A. Power to 25w.\n    * Dual-channel H-bridge design, can drive one 2-phase stepper motor, one 4-phase stepper motor or two DC motors.\n    * L298N Motor Drive Controller Board Module is ideal for Arduino, Smart Car, Power UNO, MEGA R3, Mega 2560, etc.\n    * pack 2\n\n&#34;,&#xA;    {&#xA;      size: &#34;small&#34;,&#xA;      circle: &#34;false&#34;,&#xA;      shadow: &#34;false&#34;,&#xA;      blank: &#34;true&#34;&#xA;    }&#xA;  );&#xA;} catch (e) {&#xA;  console.error(&#39;Error rendering van-list:&#39;, e);&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Demo&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
